Model / size

A general-purpose model may handle validation, extraction, routing and creative synthesis; the exact model and settings are not yet logged.

Use deterministic validation, a smaller model for extraction/routing and the stronger model only for final creative synthesis. Approve the route only after a blinded quality evaluation.

Call pattern

The workflow may run synchronously end to end; retries, resubmissions or small revisions may repeat the full chain.

Normalise inputs, add an idempotency key, cache eligible outputs, regenerate only changed sections and queue non-urgent image work.

Infrastructure / region / retention

Railway and third-party services are used, but idle utilisation, service regions, grid intensity and retention periods are not yet documented.

Test scale-to-zero/serverless execution, assess regions against GDPR/latency/carbon criteria, generate low-resolution drafts first and expire rejected/intermediate media after an approved retention period.

Retrofit audit template

Artifact

MIRA Project 3 MVP, summarised in mira_artifact_reference.md.

Primary user journey

Questionnaire submission → n8n orchestration → model/image inference → structured plan and moodboard → storage → delivery in the MIRA app.

Probable hotspots — compute and data movement

Model and image inference — probably high: variable work grows with prompts, context, output tokens, image count, resolution and regeneration.

Retries and duplicate runs — repeated work: an unchanged questionnaire or a small revision may trigger more of the workflow than necessary.

Media transfer and storage — probably medium: drafts and rejected variants may move across services and persist after their useful life.

Idle app or automation capacity — unknown: an MVP with uneven traffic may leave provisioned capacity under-used.

This ranking is an architecture-based hypothesis, not measured energy consumption.

